WEBVTT

00:01.780 --> 00:03.560
<i>Master.</i>

00:03.560 --> 00:05.620
<i>It hurts.</i>

00:05.620 --> 00:07.440
<i>Help me.</i>

00:07.440 --> 00:09.300
<i>I'm so lonely.</i>

00:09.300 --> 00:12.370
<i>Why... Why...</i>

00:31.070 --> 00:32.700
<i>It's been eight years,</i>

00:33.100 --> 00:35.840
<i>but I still remember the incident.</i>

00:45.440 --> 00:46.980
Heya, Bel!

00:46.980 --> 00:48.310
Good morning.

00:48.660 --> 00:50.140
Good morning, Kerry.

00:50.140 --> 00:52.140
We're planting onions.

00:52.140 --> 00:54.270
Could you lend us a hand?

00:54.270 --> 00:55.970
Is tomorrow okay?

00:56.360 --> 00:59.310
I'm on my way to pick some herbs
 I was asked to get.

00:59.310 --> 01:01.470
Sounds like you're busy, too.

01:01.470 --> 01:03.500
Welp, I'll see you tomorrow!

01:03.500 --> 01:04.280
Sure thing.

01:22.510 --> 01:24.060
<i>A crying baby?</i>

01:25.080 --> 01:26.820
<i>Is it a pixie's trickery?</i>

01:34.850 --> 01:36.580
I don't believe it.

01:39.930 --> 01:41.800
What's a baby doing here?

01:53.950 --> 01:55.750
<i>Hay for warding off evil spirits...</i>

01:56.620 --> 01:59.540
<i>It doesn't seem neglected or abandoned.</i>

02:00.530 --> 02:02.890
<i>Guess I've got no choice, do I?</i>

02:22.330 --> 02:26.260
Angeline, don't get lured in 
by such obvious openings.

02:26.260 --> 02:29.060
You need to predict your 
opponent's movements.

02:29.060 --> 02:29.990
You hit me.

02:29.990 --> 02:30.630
Huh?

02:30.950 --> 02:33.470
You hit me for real, Dad!

02:34.210 --> 02:37.310
But you told me not to hold back.

02:37.890 --> 02:39.290
Up.

02:39.500 --> 02:40.170
What?

02:40.170 --> 02:41.530
Pick me up!

02:42.920 --> 02:47.130
You're still such a baby even 
though you're twelve, Ange.

02:50.780 --> 02:53.150
You smell nice, Dad.

02:54.450 --> 02:56.950
All right, let's get ready for dinner.

02:56.950 --> 02:57.640
Yeah!

03:02.960 --> 03:05.690
Let's splurge a little today.

03:06.800 --> 03:09.070
I love cowberries!

03:09.990 --> 03:13.610
Now let's give thanks for 
these blessings of the land.

03:14.180 --> 03:16.300
Let's eat!

03:22.260 --> 03:23.670
I'll do it.

03:23.670 --> 03:26.460
It's all right. Your old man can handle it.

03:27.440 --> 03:30.070
I'm going to the city tomorrow.

03:30.070 --> 03:32.850
I won't be able to help you anymore.

03:34.360 --> 03:37.490
Then maybe I'll let you do it after all.

03:38.620 --> 03:39.500
Okay!

03:42.390 --> 03:44.360
<i>It's been twelve years.</i>

03:44.360 --> 03:49.320
<i>I never thought she'd choose to follow 
in my footsteps and become an adventurer.</i>

03:50.430 --> 03:52.780
I'm all done, Dad!

03:54.520 --> 03:57.580
Goodness gracious...
Your hands are still wet.

03:57.580 --> 03:58.950
Squeeze me.

04:04.000 --> 04:05.670
I'm gonna work hard.

04:05.930 --> 04:10.930
I'm gonna work hard on my own to be a
 great adventurer who protects the weak.

04:12.710 --> 04:13.690
Yeah.

04:20.760 --> 04:21.690
Ange.

04:21.960 --> 04:25.390
Nothing's more important to an
 adventurer than their own life.

04:25.390 --> 04:27.150
You musn't push yourself too hard.

04:29.010 --> 04:29.670
Okay.

04:30.370 --> 04:32.790
All right. Go on, then.

04:34.020 --> 04:35.260
I'm off!

04:49.510 --> 04:57.750
<b>My Daughter Left the Nest and Returned an S-Rank Adventurer</b>

06:10.510 --> 06:15.930
<b>Episode 1 "The Melancholy of Angeline"</b>

06:14.740 --> 06:16.080
Where are our reinforcements?

06:17.090 --> 06:18.560
Don't let it escape! After it!

06:22.910 --> 06:25.040
Keep it low, Miri!

06:25.040 --> 06:26.060
Okey doke.

06:51.470 --> 06:57.450
Wow, with one blow, she took out a wyvern 
not even Double A-rankers could handle.

06:57.450 --> 06:59.350
She's that rumored S-rank adventurer!

06:59.910 --> 07:05.870
The Black-Haired Valkyrie... Angeline!

07:07.100 --> 07:09.520
You're sure in high spirits, Ange.

07:09.520 --> 07:12.230
Is your upcoming vacation that big of a deal?

07:12.230 --> 07:14.090
You bet it is!

07:14.090 --> 07:16.710
I'm seeing my dad for the 
first time in five years!

07:16.710 --> 07:20.480
Now, I'd better hurry back
to Orphen so I can pack!

07:29.370 --> 07:31.500
Boy, it's hot.

07:31.500 --> 07:33.960
What are you doing, Mr. Bel?

07:34.750 --> 07:37.300
What am I doing? I'm weeding.

07:37.300 --> 07:40.270
Then I won't have anything to do.

07:40.270 --> 07:42.670
Well, maybe, but...

07:42.670 --> 07:45.390
More importantly, my dad's calling you.

07:45.390 --> 07:46.260
What?

07:46.670 --> 07:51.840
A traveling merchant delivered 
this letter for you from Ange.

07:51.840 --> 07:53.210
Oh, thanks.

07:53.210 --> 07:56.800
I bet you were weeding our field, weren't you?

07:56.800 --> 08:01.650
You already exterminate monsters, 
manage the woods, and instruct our kids.

08:01.650 --> 08:02.880
We're all grateful for...

08:04.340 --> 08:06.560
Fine, fine. Go ahead and read it.

08:06.560 --> 08:07.270
I will.

08:16.520 --> 08:18.460
How's Ange doing?

08:18.760 --> 08:21.800
She's taking an extended 
vacation to come visit.

08:22.700 --> 08:24.690
That's big news.

08:24.690 --> 08:27.370
We'll have to give her the royal treatment.

08:27.370 --> 08:31.430
Ange's rank S now, isn't she? 
That's supposed to be amazing, right?

08:31.430 --> 08:36.580
Yeah. It's the highest rank awarded 
by the Orphen adventurer's guild.

08:36.580 --> 08:38.200
I'm so proud of my daughter.

08:40.180 --> 08:41.920
<i>It's been five years, huh?</i>

08:43.500 --> 08:45.030
<i>I'm looking forward to it.</i>

08:46.870 --> 08:50.010
I'm going home, I'm going home!

08:50.010 --> 08:53.050
Gonna get to see my dear old dad!

08:53.050 --> 08:56.210
Just how much does she love her dad?

08:56.210 --> 08:58.550
Seriously. I'm kind of surprised.

08:59.150 --> 09:01.270
You two sure you won't come?

09:01.270 --> 09:07.430
We haev to temporarily work with another
 party as a condition for your vacation.

09:07.430 --> 09:11.600
Though I <i>am</i> curious to find out 
what your dad's like.

09:12.870 --> 09:15.440
He's kind, strong, and incredibly cool.

09:15.440 --> 09:17.110
I'm proud to call him my father.

09:17.110 --> 09:20.680
He's strong? Is he an adventurer, too?

09:20.680 --> 09:22.910
Yeah. Well, a former one, anyway.

09:22.910 --> 09:27.120
He taught me how to use a sword and 
everything I know about being an adventurer.

09:27.120 --> 09:28.380
Wow.

09:29.320 --> 09:33.130
I still haven't managed
to land a blow on him yet.

09:33.130 --> 09:35.250
What? You haven't?

09:35.250 --> 09:36.870
Then he must be amazing!

09:36.870 --> 09:40.990
He is! My dad is absolutely the best!

09:43.640 --> 09:45.940
H-Hey, Ms. Ange...

09:46.520 --> 09:48.250
Mr. Lionel.

09:48.250 --> 09:50.790
What brings the guild master to my door?

09:51.270 --> 09:57.150
W-Well, you see, a swarm of giga ants and
 their queen have turned up in Asterinos...

09:57.950 --> 10:00.240
I've already submitted my request for time off!

10:00.240 --> 10:01.510
I'm going home to Turnera!

10:01.510 --> 10:02.870
Won't you reconsider?!

10:04.420 --> 10:08.540
People have already died... Please help them!

10:12.200 --> 10:15.630
If we don't go,
Asterinos is as good as done for.

10:15.630 --> 10:18.580
It's too bad, but... y'know?

10:30.060 --> 10:32.420
Pesky insects...

10:33.440 --> 10:35.750
I'll kill every last one of you!

10:45.300 --> 10:46.590
Ange!

10:48.600 --> 10:51.380
Is this the home of Mr. Belgrieve?

10:51.740 --> 10:54.390
Yes, that's me.

10:54.390 --> 10:57.560
I have a letter from Ms. Angeline.

10:58.520 --> 11:00.500
Thank you.

11:08.020 --> 11:11.840
I see. An urgent job, huh?

11:14.760 --> 11:17.530
<i>I hope I get to see her soon.</i>

11:26.420 --> 11:28.870
Ange's pretty irritated, huh?

11:28.870 --> 11:32.410
No helping it.
Her vacation got put off again.

11:39.950 --> 11:42.890
<i>I hope I get to see my dad soon...</i>

11:50.770 --> 11:52.950
What incredible speed...

11:52.950 --> 11:55.740
I can't believe she's 
completed this many jobs.

11:55.740 --> 11:59.730
Ms. Angeline must've just been 
in that much of a hurry to go home.

12:12.000 --> 12:14.000
You're in a rather good mood.

12:14.000 --> 12:16.630
Judging by your luggage, 
are you on your way home?

12:16.630 --> 12:19.120
I am, at long last.

12:19.120 --> 12:21.140
It's been a week since I left Orphen.

12:21.140 --> 12:22.380
I'm almost there.

12:22.380 --> 12:27.290
Sorry for asking you to guard 
my goods during your time off.

12:27.290 --> 12:31.210
It's fine. My trip home was postponed
 because of an urgent job,

12:31.210 --> 12:33.100
but I finally get to see my dad.

12:33.100 --> 12:35.790
I'm sure your father will be delighted.

12:36.340 --> 12:40.760
Say, my dad's known as Belgrieve the Red Ogre.

12:40.760 --> 12:41.790
Ever heard of him?

12:41.790 --> 12:45.250
Pardon my ignorance.
I'll remember that name.

12:45.250 --> 12:49.720
But only exceptional adventurers 
earn titles like that.

12:49.720 --> 12:52.000
I bet he's impressively powerful.

12:52.260 --> 12:56.760
Yeah. I'm proud of my dad, 
Belgrieve the Red Ogre.

12:58.530 --> 13:01.200
Mr. Belgrieve the Red Ogre, huh?

13:01.200 --> 13:03.000
Must be something...

13:08.120 --> 13:09.940
Wait... What?

13:15.310 --> 13:17.830
Please let us go.

13:17.830 --> 13:20.310
I'm in a race against time.

13:21.060 --> 13:22.020
What?

13:22.020 --> 13:26.940
If you don't want to die,
leave the girl and get out of here.

13:26.940 --> 13:30.250
Ha! Can't you see how many of us there are?

13:30.250 --> 13:32.160
What can you do all by yourself?

13:32.160 --> 13:33.070
You'll pay.

13:33.070 --> 13:33.710
What?

13:34.030 --> 13:35.700
Because of you...

13:36.890 --> 13:39.710
I'll have less time with my dad now.

13:41.280 --> 13:43.020
Wh-What's with her?

13:44.040 --> 13:47.090
I'll make you pay for this!

13:55.980 --> 13:57.880
A-Are you all right?!

13:57.880 --> 14:01.310
Yes. Some bandits were attacking 
this girl and her guard.

14:01.310 --> 14:02.590
Honestly...

14:03.240 --> 14:06.460
Thank you for saving us.

14:06.460 --> 14:10.740
I am the third daughter of 
the Bordeaux family, Seren.

14:10.740 --> 14:14.000
What? You're a daughter of Count Bordeaux?

14:14.300 --> 14:18.080
Someone so important 
should have more guards...

14:18.080 --> 14:20.920
While touring the area, I got word

14:20.920 --> 14:23.840
that my father collapsed 
and is in critical condition.

14:24.430 --> 14:29.100
I rode out to see him as quickly as 
I could with only my guard at the time.

14:30.070 --> 14:31.730
You're going to see your father?

14:32.090 --> 14:35.550
Since we've now lost our horses...

14:35.550 --> 14:39.340
It's more than a four-day walk to Bordeaux.

14:42.300 --> 14:44.910
I doubt I'll make it in time.

14:46.850 --> 14:51.300
But it wouldn't be right to ask
since you saved my life...

14:52.660 --> 14:54.610
This must be fate.

14:55.070 --> 14:56.340
What are you saying?!

14:56.880 --> 14:58.970
This is your dear father we're talking about.

14:58.970 --> 15:01.140
Don't just chalk it up to fate!

15:02.180 --> 15:03.550
Ms. Angeline...

15:04.120 --> 15:06.290
Take us back to Bordeaux immediately.

15:06.290 --> 15:10.790
What? B-But Ms. Angeline, your father...

15:10.790 --> 15:13.780
I need to take this girl 
to her see her sick father.

15:14.300 --> 15:17.440
I'll pay for your goods and your trouble.

15:17.440 --> 15:19.430
So please.

15:21.120 --> 15:23.930
Get in. We'll go as fast as we can.

15:27.810 --> 15:30.450
Thank you so very much.

15:32.910 --> 15:38.120
<i>I'm sorry, Dad, but I'll make it home
 next time for sure.</i>

15:43.630 --> 15:46.420
I see. So that's what happened.

15:46.900 --> 15:48.700
She sure is working hard.

15:48.700 --> 15:50.360
Mr. Bel!

15:50.360 --> 15:52.160
Let's go to the mountains!

15:54.440 --> 15:56.630
Is it that time already?

15:56.630 --> 16:00.690
Sorry. The kids insisted we come now.

16:02.360 --> 16:04.930
I'll get ready. Give me a minute.

16:10.670 --> 16:13.820
Listen up. We're not here to play.

16:13.820 --> 16:16.060
Pay attention to your surroundings.

16:16.060 --> 16:17.630
Okay!

16:17.630 --> 16:20.090
Pete, how are things up front?

16:20.540 --> 16:23.200
Don't just look. Use all of your senses.

16:24.190 --> 16:28.510
I hear the trees swaying in the wind, 
the sound of flowing water, and...

16:29.590 --> 16:33.220
There's a pleasant, refreshing smell.

16:33.520 --> 16:35.750
That's the scent of devil's dropwort.

16:36.220 --> 16:39.370
It's an herb that only grows 
where there's clean water.

16:40.100 --> 16:42.460
It means there's a watering hole nearby.

16:42.460 --> 16:44.360
Whoa...

16:44.360 --> 16:46.720
Okay, let's find that watering hole.

16:46.970 --> 16:50.560
But don't focus solely on that.

16:50.560 --> 16:54.210
We could run into beasts or
 monsters at any moment.

16:54.210 --> 16:55.500
Okay!

16:59.990 --> 17:03.150
Let's gather devil's dropwort, everyone.

17:03.150 --> 17:06.070
But don't wander off too far.

17:06.070 --> 17:07.240
Okay!

17:08.040 --> 17:09.500
Let's start over there.

17:09.500 --> 17:11.540
What's it look like?

17:12.180 --> 17:16.440
<i>Come to think of it, 
I came here often with Ange.</i>

17:16.440 --> 17:19.470
<i>She learned everything 
after seeing it just once.</i>

17:20.090 --> 17:22.540
<i>Dad, this is it, right?</i>

17:22.540 --> 17:24.890
<i>Sure is. Nicely spotted.</i>

17:27.080 --> 17:31.090
<i>Feels like it was more
than just a child's quick wit.</i>

17:31.720 --> 17:33.960
<i>Go figure she made it to rank S.</i>

17:34.410 --> 17:38.450
<i>In contrast, I'm just a wannabe quitter.</i>

17:39.480 --> 17:40.770
<i>I...</i>

17:41.440 --> 17:47.200
<i>No, I wouldn't have found Ange 
if I hadn't returned to Orphen.</i>

17:48.440 --> 17:50.490
<i>What will be, will be.</i>

17:54.530 --> 17:55.340
Oh, no!

18:09.850 --> 18:11.310
Mr. Bel?

18:11.310 --> 18:12.390
Are you all right?

18:13.300 --> 18:15.250
That was lame.

18:15.250 --> 18:19.230
I doubt this would've happened to Ange...

18:24.740 --> 18:27.030
She's really stressed out.

18:27.030 --> 18:28.500
Seriously.

18:28.500 --> 18:31.990
I'm gonna work so hard that the next 
time I take an extended vacation,

18:31.990 --> 18:34.510
the guild won't be able to say a word!

18:34.510 --> 18:38.810
Say, say! If you're feeling stressed,
 I know a nice place.

18:38.810 --> 18:40.290
Why don't we all go?

18:40.290 --> 18:41.520
Huh?

18:47.980 --> 18:50.040
Can we finish all of this?

18:53.920 --> 18:55.270
It's so good!

18:56.450 --> 18:58.680
I'm so happy.

18:59.030 --> 19:02.270
It's not too sweet or greasy.

19:02.950 --> 19:04.830
It's tasty!

19:04.830 --> 19:06.450
It's the best!

19:06.450 --> 19:08.020
It's certainly good.

19:08.860 --> 19:11.360
Ane, if you don't want that, can I have it?

19:11.360 --> 19:13.660
Nope. This is mine.

19:14.260 --> 19:16.860
I wish my dad could try this.

19:17.160 --> 19:19.450
It's too bad about the other day.

19:19.450 --> 19:22.180
You haven't been home yet, right?

19:22.180 --> 19:26.190
Right. I don't know when 
I'll be able to take time off next.

19:26.570 --> 19:31.040
But didn't you save a daughter 
of Count Bordeaux?

19:31.040 --> 19:33.390
Yeah, apparently.

19:33.390 --> 19:37.310
He governs land in the north
that includes Turnera.

19:37.310 --> 19:40.830
I'm impressed you made a connection
with such an influential noble.

19:41.520 --> 19:44.190
I don't care about that.

19:44.630 --> 19:48.070
I'm just glad Seren got to see her dad.

19:49.210 --> 19:50.180
I see.

19:52.260 --> 19:54.570
Next time, I'll make it home.

19:54.840 --> 19:57.210
If I keep up this pace,

19:57.210 --> 20:01.200
the guild won't be able to decline
my next extended vacation request.

20:03.100 --> 20:09.190
At least we're raking in the money 
since we do nothing but work.

20:09.190 --> 20:13.930
If you've got more than you know what 
to do with, why not give to the orphanage?

20:13.930 --> 20:17.470
Oh, you're so right.
The sister would be delighted.

20:18.290 --> 20:19.480
The orphanage?

20:19.480 --> 20:21.970
We grew up in an orphanage.

20:21.970 --> 20:24.850
The sister was like a mother to us.

20:24.850 --> 20:27.750
I guess we didn't have a father.

20:28.190 --> 20:30.440
I never knew that.

20:30.440 --> 20:32.890
We never talk about our life stories.

20:34.120 --> 20:35.600
You're right.

20:35.600 --> 20:39.740
We're always talking about 
monsters or adventurers.

20:40.430 --> 20:42.070
I was abandoned as a baby.

20:42.740 --> 20:45.010
My dad found me in the mountains.

20:45.840 --> 20:46.760
What?

20:47.860 --> 20:50.690
For real? Seriously? Tell us more!

20:53.510 --> 20:57.630
<i>Dear Dad... I'm sorry I haven't 
been able to come home.</i>

20:58.590 --> 21:02.320
<i>After reaching rank S,
I joined my first party.</i>

21:03.240 --> 21:07.140
<i>At first I wasn't sure about 
adventuring with companions,</i>

21:07.140 --> 21:09.320
<i>but now I find they're quite dependable.</i>

21:10.120 --> 21:12.810
<i>Anessa is the oldest and very serious.</i>

21:13.490 --> 21:16.830
<i>She never misses with her bow.</i>

21:17.430 --> 21:20.320
<i>She handles all the troublesome 
negotiating that comes with jobs.</i>

21:21.270 --> 21:23.670
<i>Miriam is a year older than me.</i>

21:23.670 --> 21:26.090
<i>She's a mage skilled in lightning magic.</i>

21:26.560 --> 21:30.330
<i>Even though she's shorter than me,
 she's better endowed.</i>

21:30.330 --> 21:34.840
<i>It's frustrating, but I have faith in myself.
I'm still growing!</i>

21:36.100 --> 21:42.210
<i>Still, I'd rather speak with you in 
person than write you letters.</i>

21:44.610 --> 21:47.670
<i>There's so much I can't fit in writing
that I hardly know what to do.</i>

21:48.320 --> 21:50.080
<i>I miss you.</i>

21:50.600 --> 21:52.550
<i>I'm sure I'll make it home next time.</i>

21:53.120 --> 21:54.550
<i>Wait for me.</i>

21:58.360 --> 22:02.300
I miss you too, Ange.

23:35.100 --> 23:40.050
<b>Next Time</b>

23:35.100 --> 23:40.050
<b>"Belgrieve the Red Ogre"</b>
